A third path exists: VENDORED code. `vendor/surrealdb-kvs-test/` is upstream's
shared key-value backend contract suite, `surrealdb/kvs-test` at tag v3.3.0
(commit 238bfeb), copied in verbatim and unmodified. It is `publish = false`, so
there is no other way to link it. It is BUSL-1.1 (`vendor/surrealdb-kvs-test/LICENSE`),
it is marked BUSL-1.1 in its own manifest, and it is the one place in this
repository where SurrealDB source code is a build input. Vendoring it is
recorded as a decision in DECISIONS.md (ADR-0005); the wider firewall — that
`upstream/surrealdb/` is a reference and never a build input — is unchanged.

